-The call paragraph begins **“At approximately9:30am or9:45am on09/11/01”** (spacing regularized only for readability; the **or**, two values and approximate qualification are retained). It reports a hijacking conversation, a number supplied for a callback, screaming and the line going dead. The next paragraph says the attempted callback got a message that the number was not in service. It then expressly says the recipient **assumed** Britton had borrowed a cellphone, given the number she supplied. This is an inference reported in an interview, not direct observation of the onboard equipment or an independently verified service classification.
